UID:canon-foundation-europe-research-fellowships-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Canon Foundation in Europe Research Fellowships 2026 (Eur
 ope–Japan Exchange)
DESCRIPTION:Canon Foundation in Europe Research Fellowships support bilater
 al research exchange between Europe and Japan\, awarding up to 15 fellowsh
 ips annually. AMOUNT: up to EUR 30\,000 per year (pro-rated for shorter st
 ays)\, flexible — covers living costs\, travel\, insurance\, research ex
 penses\, and books\; fellows determine their own allocation. ELIGIBILITY: 
 European nationals (including UK\, Israel\, Switzerland\, Turkey\, Balkan 
 and Baltic countries) conducting research in Japan\; or Japanese nationals
  conducting research in Europe. Applicants must have completed at least a 
 Master's or PhD degree within the last 10 years (older qualifications may 
 apply with supporting documentation). No restrictions on research field. P
 riority given to first-time applicants to Europe/Japan. Fellows arrange th
 eir own host institution and advisor. Up to 15 fellowships awarded annuall
 y. Deadline: 15 September 2026\, 23:59 CET (for fellowships starting Janua
 ry-December 2027). Apply at https://portal.canonfoundation.org/. Contact: 
 canon.foundation@canon-europe.com.\n\nOrganisation: Canon Foundation in Eu
 rope\nLocation: Europe or Japan (bilateral exchange\; fellows arrange own 
 host institution)\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000 per year (pro-rated for shorte
 r stays). No application fee.\nDuration: Minimum 3 months\, maximum 1 year
 . Fellowships for 2027 start.\n\nMore: https://portal.canonfoundation.org/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://portal.canonfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe or Japan (bilateral exchange\; fellows arrange own host ins
 titution)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-get-ready-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, will open its fifth call from 1 September to 3 November 2026\, wit
 h full guidelines and application details published on 1 September 2026. C
 all #5 will again support around 50 cross-border co-production residencies
  taking place in 2027\, each bringing together at least three festivals fr
 om different eligible countries to accompany an emerging artist or collect
 ive. EFFEA is a co-production residency scheme: festivals join forces acro
 ss borders to support an emerging artist through a process of creation and
  presentation\, providing dedicated time\, space\, and tailored mentoring\
 , exchange\, and collaboration\, moving beyond a single invitation toward 
 a shared artistic development journey. Each supported project is built aro
 und one leading festival working with at least two partner festivals based
  in different eligible countries\; one emerging artist or collective at th
 e centre\; a combination of artistic development\, mentoring\, exchange\, 
 and audience engagement based on the artist's needs\; and presentations or
  outcomes shared across the partner festivals. Two residency formats are o
 ffered. DISCOVERY (EUR 8\,000 grant): the proposal must include a workshop
  (live or online) hosted by the leading festival with at least one program
 mer from each partner festival\, and a work-in-progress presentation at th
 e leading festival. SPRINGBOARD (EUR 15\,000 grant): the proposal must inc
 lude final presentations or production results shown within each festival 
 (minimum the leading festival plus two partners) and a live masterclass le
 d by the artist(s) at each festival (minimum the leading festival plus two
  partners). WHO CAN APPLY: festivals that have existed for at least one ed
 ition and are registered on FestivalFinder.eu\; the festivals apply on beh
 alf of the residency project. Residency projects must fall within these ar
 tistic fields: architecture\, ballet\, contemporary dance\, circus\, desig
 n/applied arts\, digital arts\, film\, folklore and folk arts\, heritage\,
  interdisciplinary\, literature\, music\, opera\, street art\, theatre\, p
 hotography/video\, puppetry\, sculpture\, painting. A series of EFFEA info
 \, networking\, and Q&A sessions runs on Tuesdays 11:00-12:00 CEST (15 Sep
 tember\, 29 September\, 13 October\, and 20 October 2026) to help applican
 ts navigate the process and find partners. Across Calls #1 to #4\, EFFEA h
 as supported 619 festivals and 200 artists/collectives across Europe and b
 eyond.\n\nOrganisation: European Festivals Association (EFA)\nLocation: Ac
 ross eligible European countries\; residencies built around partner festiv
 als registered on FestivalFinder.eu\nAward: Per-residency grants: EUR 8\,0
 00 (Discovery format) or EUR 15\,000 (Springboard format)\nDuration: Resid
 encies take place in 2027\; call open 1 September to 3 November 2026\, ful
 l guidelines published 1 September 2026\n\nMore: https://www.effea.eu/news
 /item/2026/06/24/effea-call-5-get-ready?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.effea.eu/news/item/2026/06/24/effea-call-5-get-ready?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Across eligible European countries\; residencies built around part
 ner festivals registered on FestivalFinder.eu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rijkscultuurfondsen-interdisciplinary-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rijkscultuurfondsen: Interdisciplinary Grant
DESCRIPTION:The Interdisciplinary grant is a new joint scheme of the six Du
 tch national cultural funds (Mondriaan Fund\, Performing Arts Fund NL\, Fu
 nd for Cultural Participation\, Netherlands Film Fund\, Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL\, and the Dutch Foundation for Literature)\, announced on 7 July
  2026. It supports makers and organisations whose work genuinely crosses t
 he boundaries of the individual funds' disciplines (visual art\, design\, 
 film\, literature\, performing arts\, and cultural participation) and cann
 ot be contained within a single discipline. TWO TRACKS: an Individual trac
 k for professional makers with a demonstrable interdisciplinary practice (
 at least one year of experience\; income cap EUR 55\,000 including the gra
 nt\; approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months)\; and an Organisation track 
 for organisations running multi-discipline projects. AMOUNT: EUR 12\,500 t
 o 50\,000 per project. ELIGIBILITY: makers and organisations based in the 
 Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. APPLYING: handled throug
 h the Mondriaan Fund's online application portal (info@mondriaanfonds.nl)\
 ; an account is required in advance. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026\, 16:00 Dutc
 h time (single application round).\n\nOrganisation: Dutch national cultura
 l funds (Rijkscultuurfondsen)\, via the Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Netherla
 nds. For professional makers and organisations based in the Netherlands or
  the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans multiple disciplin
 es.\nAward: EUR 12\,500 to 50\,000 per project. The individual-maker track
  is approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months (income cap EUR 55\,000 includ
 ing the grant).\nDuration: Up to 12 months for the individual-maker track.
 \n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interd
 isciplinary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interdiscipli
 nary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. For professional makers and organisations based in th
 e Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans mu
 ltiple disciplines.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:institut-francais-cite-internationale-des-arts-2027-2028@artificialnouv
 eau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:Deadline: Institut francais x Cite internationale des arts Residenc
 ies 2027-2028
DESCRIPTION:Residency programme run by the Institut francais de Paris with 
 the Cite internationale des arts\, one of France's largest international a
 rtist mobility programmes\, supporting nearly seventy artists and cultural
  professionals each year. It offers furnished individual live-work studios
  in the Marais for 3\, 6 or 9 months across four quarterly windows between
  April 2027 and April 2028 (arrivals 9 April 2027\, 9 July 2027\, 8 Octobe
 r 2027\, or 7 January 2028)\, plus access to an auditorium\, exhibition sp
 aces\, rehearsal studios and shared printmaking\, screen-printing and cera
 mics workshops. The Institut francais covers the monthly cost of the studi
 o\; the artist's nominating partner organisation submits the application a
 nd must provide a stipend of at least EUR 1\,100 per month plus internatio
 nal travel\, insurance and visa fees. ELIGIBILITY: established artists and
  cultural professionals of any nationality who have lived outside France f
 or at least 5 years\, with an active professional practice\, a clearly def
 ined research or creative project\, and professional-level French and/or E
 nglish\; open across disciplines (theatre\, dance\, performance\, visual a
 rts\, music\, literature\, cinema\, architecture\, design\, digital creati
 on\, photography\, fashion\, crafts\, curating\, and more). IMPORTANT: art
 ists cannot apply directly - a partner organisation (French cultural netwo
 rk abroad\, or a French or foreign cultural organisation) must nominate an
 d support the applicant\, committing financial and professional support be
 fore\, during and after the residency. Applications open 1 July 2026\; fre
 e to apply. Deadline: 8 October 2026\, 11:59 PM CET.\n\nOrganisation: Inst
 itut francais de Paris (with Cite internationale des arts)\nLocation: Pari
 s\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Marais\, 18 rue de l'Hotel de V
 ille\, 4th arrondissement)\nAward: Furnished\, Wi-Fi-equipped studio apart
 ment in Paris with monthly costs covered by the Institut francais. The nom
 inating partner organisation must provide a residency stipend of at least 
 EUR 1\,100 per month and cover the artist's international travel\, insuran
 ce (health\, repatriation\, liability) and any visa fees. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: 3\, 6\, or 9 months (1 to 3 consecutive quarters) between A
 pril 2027 and April 2028\n\nMore: https://www.institutfrancais.com/en/prog
 ramme/residence-and-professional-mobility/residencies-institut-francais-x-
 cite-internationale?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.institutfrancais.com/en/programme/residence-and-professiona
 l-mobility/residencies-institut-francais-x-cite-internationale?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Marais\, 18 rue de 
 l'Hotel de Ville\, 4th arrondissement)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adagp-sgdl-arcane-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arcane Grant 2026 for Artist Books
DESCRIPTION:Artists' books get little support\, financially or in distribut
 ion\, despite their place in art history and in the careers of the people 
 who make them. ADAGP\, the French collecting society for copyright in the 
 visual arts\, and SGDL\, the French society of authors\, created the Arcan
 e grant in response: EUR 9\,000 to one winning project for the conception 
 and production of an artist's book made collaboratively by a visual artist
  and a writer. WHO CAN APPLY: a pair consisting of a professional visual a
 rtist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at least fi
 ve years\, or a French national living abroad) and a French-language autho
 r working in fiction\, non-fiction\, poetry\, children's literature or the
 atre who has already been published by a publisher. A trio is also possibl
 e where a publishing structure joins the project. WHAT COUNTS AS AN ARTIST
 'S BOOK: a creation\, a work of art in book form\, in a limited print run 
 of between 1 and 500 copies\, which may be signed or numbered. Explicitly 
 not eligible: magazines\, fanzines\, limited editions of an ordinary book\
 , and any publication that simply presents an artist's work\, such as mono
 graphs or illustrated books. APPLICATION: the file must be in French and i
 ncludes a jointly written project presentation of up to three pages coveri
 ng the artistic and editorial vision\, constituent elements\, methods of r
 ealisation and desired final form\; a one-page technical sheet giving titl
 e\, print run\, format\, page count\, paper quality\, printing techniques 
 and materials\; a provisional timetable\; and a detailed balanced provisio
 nal budget of expenses and financing. Artistic elements are a CV of exhibi
 tions and publications (2 pages) and a portfolio with website link (10 pag
 es) for the artist\, a CV and website link for the author (2 pages)\, and 
 a one-page editorial line for the publishing structure if there is one\; c
 ontact details must be omitted from these. Administrative elements are swo
 rn declarations that the project is a new creation with copyright held sol
 ely by the pair\, that the artist is from the French scene\, and\, if appl
 icable\, that the publishing structure undertakes to publish the work. Tem
 plates are downloadable from the Required Documents page. TIMELINE: call l
 aunched 7 July 2026\, applications close 7 September 2026 at 2pm\, jury me
 ets November 2026\, winner announced end of November 2026\, and the work m
 ust be published within two years of that announcement. The regulations mu
 st be read before applying\, and submitting an application constitutes acc
 eptance of them. Contact: arcane@adagp.fr.\n\nOrganisation: ADAGP and SGDL
  (Societe des Gens de Lettres)\nLocation: France. Open to a professional v
 isual artist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at l
 east five years\, or of French nationality living abroad) paired with a Fr
 ench-language author.\nAward: EUR 9\,000 to the single winning project\, s
 upporting the conception and production of an artist's book. NOTE ON TAX: 
 ADAGP grants count as primary artistic income under the French Intellectua
 l Property Code (art. L112-2)\, so the sum falls under the artist-author s
 ocial security and tax regime\, subject to URSSAF contributions and income
  tax declared as non-commercial profits (micro-BNC or controlled declarati
 on). VAT is not due. No application fee.\nDuration: The winning duo or tri
 o commits to publishing the artist's book within two years of the announce
 ment\n\nMore: https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=pr
 ogramme&cid=187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=programme&cid
 =187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:France. Open to a professional visual artist from the French scene
  (working or residing in France for at least five years\, or of French nat
 ionality living abroad) paired with a French-language author.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:linz-kultur-arbeitsstipendien-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Linz Kultur Working Grants 2026 (Arbeitsstipendien)
DESCRIPTION:The city of Linz awards project-related working grants to susta
 in and develop its art scene\, in line with the Linz cultural development 
 plan and the city's status as a UNESCO City of Media Arts. The stated aims
  are enabling the further development of artistic practice\, supporting ar
 tistic careers\, and securing a professional artistic existence and innova
 tive production in Linz. Each scholarship is worth EUR 5\,000 over five mo
 nths\, with EUR 30\,000 available in total this year. DISCIPLINES: fine ar
 ts and photography\, literature\, music\, performing arts\, interdisciplin
 ary art forms\, media art and film. WHAT TO SUBMIT: a concrete artistic pr
 oject\, which may be an independent work\, a series of works\, or the cont
 inuation of an earlier series or project. Preparatory work and concept pha
 ses are also eligible. Projects already funded by the City of Linz cannot 
 be submitted\, and only one submission per person per year is permitted. E
 LIGIBILITY: artists of any citizenship who can demonstrate that their cent
 re of work is in Linz\, in the form of a permanent site for their artistic
  work\, and who have a sufficient connection to the city. SELECTION CRITER
 IA: the expert jury assesses sufficient Linz connection\, innovative artis
 tic potential\, independent artistic expression\, a clearly recognisable c
 onception of the artistic intention in the proposal\, and the quality and 
 continuity of the artistic work. REPORTING OBLIGATION: within three months
  of the scholarship ending\, a written progress report of 1\,800 to 5\,400
  characters including spaces must be submitted with supporting documentati
 on\, and after review it is published on the City of Linz website. The pro
 ject need not be finished\, but significant progress must be evident. If n
 o report is submitted\, or the report shows insufficient progress\, the sc
 holarship must be repaid under the City of Linz General Funding Guidelines
 . REQUIRED DOCUMENTS: the completed online application form\, a project de
 scription of up to 10 pages including the innovative approach and planned 
 schedule\, a biography with catalogue of works and any exhibition or prese
 ntation list\, an artistic portfolio\, and references and press reviews. N
 OTE: the online form and the call documents are in German. Contact: lkf.kb
 @mag.linz.at. Deadline 7 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: City of Linz (Li
 nz Kultur\, Arts and Cultural Funding Department)\nLocation: Linz\, Austri
 a. Open to artists of any citizenship whose centre of work is in Linz.\nAw
 ard: EUR 5\,000 per scholarship over a five-month period\, from a total po
 t of EUR 30\,000 this year\, so approximately six grants. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Five months\n\nMore: https://www.linz.at/serviceguide/viewc
 hapter.php?chapter_id=123406&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.linz.at/serviceguide/viewchapter.php?chapter_id=123406&utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Linz\, Austria. Open to artists of any citizenship whose centre of
  work is in Linz.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultural-horizons-residencies-subgrants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260827T221858Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultural Horizons Residencies: Subgrants for EU-Ukrainian
  Residency Projects 2027
DESCRIPTION:Cultural Horizons strengthens the cultural sector in Ukraine by
  promoting joint EU-Ukrainian cultural initiatives and expanding access fo
 r Ukrainians affected by the war to cultural and artistic networks in Euro
 pe. Running 2026 to 2027\, it provides subgrants for projects developed th
 rough EU-Ukrainian partnerships and builds a Europe-wide network of cultur
 al expert mentors. THIS CALL\, the Residencies strand\, gives subgrants to
  EU-based institutions to run (a) residency placements and/or (b) educatio
 n projects organised on the basis of residencies\, for and with Ukrainian 
 artistic and cultural professionals during 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic a
 nd cultural organisations and initiatives registered within the EU. Consor
 tium applications are allowed but must designate one lead organisation to 
 submit and manage the funding. This is an organisational call\, so individ
 ual Ukrainian artists cannot apply directly\; they participate as the host
 ed residents. Applicants must show they can host Ukrainian professionals i
 n 2027 and complete the project in the stated window. NGOs and public sect
 or institutions working with displaced and vulnerable groups are prioritis
 ed. CONDITIONS: applicants must confirm the absence of ties with the Russi
 an Federation\, meaning no working partnerships with Russia or Russian org
 anisations and no visits to Russian-occupied territories after 2014\, comm
 it to refrain from the glorification of Russian imperialism\, and comply w
 ith the EU sanctions regime. They must also demonstrate a commitment to di
 versity\, equity and inclusion and provide a working environment based on 
 mutual trust\, awareness and intercultural sensitivity. WHO THE MONEY IS M
 EANT TO REACH: Ukrainian artists and cultural practitioners\, whether inde
 pendent or employed\, including early-career specialists\, debut artists\,
  cultural managers\, researchers\, analysts and conservators\; vulnerable 
 groups from Ukraine including internally displaced persons\, young artists
 \, and communities in frontline and conflict-affected areas\; and cultural
  organisations in Ukraine\, with particular focus on small communities\, l
 ocal initiatives\, independent cultural spaces and NGOs. APPLYING: submiss
 ion is through a JotForm hosted by Cultural Vistas and must be complete\, 
 including uploads\, or it will not be processed. You should receive an ema
 il confirmation\; if it does not arrive\, the submission was not received.
  Enquiries to culturalhorizons@culturalvistas.eu. NOTE ON DATES: the eligi
 bility section says projects must be completed within January to August 20
 27 while the application instructions give the implementation phase as 1 J
 anuary to 30 July 2027\, so plan to the earlier end date. Programme backgr
 ound is at culturalvistas.eu under Our Programs\, Professional Study Tours
 \, Cultural Horizons.\n\nOrganisation: Ukrainian Cultural Foundation and C
 ultural Vistas\, funded by the Creative Europe programme of the European U
 nion\nLocation: Applicant organisations must be registered in the EU. Resi
 dencies are hosted in the EU for Ukrainian artistic and cultural professio
 nals.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000 per subgrant\, with a minimum of 20 su
 bgrants to be awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects run between
  1 January and 30 July 2027\, minimum 3 months and maximum 8 months. Appli
 cations 29 June to 30 September 2026\; evaluation October to November 2026
 . Final reports are due within one month of project completion and no late
 r than 15 August 2027.\n\nMore: https://culturalvistas.jotform.com/2617534
 20662859?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
